    "summary": [
      {
        "value": "Runting-stunting syndrome is a growth problem seen in broiler chickens since the 1940s, where a portion of the flock grows poorly and converts feed less efficiently, usually becoming obvious around 30 to 42 days old. It has been linked to several viruses (especially reovirus) and bacteria acting together, and while reovirus vaccines and good hygiene help, the condition often clears up on its own.",
